<li><a href="https://www.intralox.com/belt-finder/modular-plastic-belting/series-800/flat-top" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Series 800 Flat Top belt data</a>, Intralox. Temperature ranges by belt resin.</li>
<li><a href="https://bulkinside.com/bulk-solids-handling/mechanical-conveying/technical-guidance-series-part-one-abrasion/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Technical Guidance Series Part One: Abrasion</a>, Fenner Dunlop via Bulk Inside. ISO 4649 abrasion test and DIN/ISO grade families.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.fennerdunlopemea.com/app/uploads/emea-product-range-en__digital.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Conveyor Belting Product Range</a>, Fenner Dunlop EMEA. DIN Y, X, W meanings, DIN Y abrasion limit, and DIN/ISO grade mapping.</li>
<li><a href="https://fennerdunlopamericas.com/compound-attribute/cut-gouge-arpm-grade-i/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cut/Gouge Resistance (ARPM Grade I) compounds</a> and <a href="https://fennerdunlopamericas.com/compound-attribute/abrasion-arpm-grade-ii/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Abrasion Resistance (ARPM Grade II) compounds</a>, Fenner Dunlop Americas. ARPM grade families.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What are the main types of conveyor belt material?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Six main types: PVC (general-purpose, lowest cost), polyurethane (food-grade, abrasion resistant), silicone (high heat, non-stick), rubber (heavy-duty grip and impact), modular plastic (repairable, sprocket-driven), and metal (ovens, freezers, heavy loads). Selection depends on product contact, temperature, chemicals, incline, uptime, and budget.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What belt material is FDA-approved for food?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Polyurethane, silicone, some PVC formulations, acetal and polypropylene modular plastics, and stainless steel are available in food-contact formulations. The FDA clearance varies by material and food type, so ask the belt maker which regulation or clearance applies. Polyurethane is widely specified because it combines compliance, abrasion resistance, and easy cleaning. USDA acceptance also depends on smooth, cleanable belt construction. Blue and white colors aid visual <a href="/conveyor-functions/inspection-detection/">contamination detection</a>.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">Which belt material is most abrasion resistant?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Among polymer belts, rubber and polyurethane. For rubber, ask for the cover grade: DIN W and ISO D are the high-abrasion grades, and ARPM Grade II is the North American abrasion grade. In modular plastic belts, acetal is hard and wear resistant, abrasion-resistant nylon grades are offered for severe wear, and polypropylene trades some wear resistance for chemical resistance. Metal belts resist abrasion best but cost more. Ask suppliers for wear data on your product.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">How long does a conveyor belt last?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>It depends on material, product abrasion, speed, tension, cleaning chemicals, temperature, and maintenance. Modular plastic belts often last longest in service because damaged modules are replaced individually. Tracking, tensioning, and cleaning matter as much as material, and a mistracking belt can be destroyed quickly. See the <a href="/resources/conveyor-maintenance/">maintenance guide</a> for procedures.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5">What is a modular conveyor belt?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-5" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Interlocking plastic modules joined by hinge rods. Damaged modules are replaced without removing the belt. Sprocket drive means no tracking problems. Food-grade acetal, polypropylene, and polyethylene are standard. Higher upfront cost than flat belts, with less repair time and downtime.</p>

</div>
